  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I'm working on a prefab and I have been struggling between prioritizing UI or Information.\n\nWhen there is more than 5 toggles/menus/buttons in the Action Menu, there is less space for text and keeping buttons informative are hard if we can't get or make the right descriptive icons that tells everything or enough about a toggle/menu.\n\nBesides shape, relying on colored icons is useless if a user is color blind. So 1 shape and 1 word is all I can put in 1 slot.\n\nBut what if there was a Tool Tip somewhere around the Action Menu where I can put up to 6 words or something to give more information about the toggle? That would be amazing!\n\nThis speeds up and simplifies the understanding of a menu for a user without having to be in front of the mirror or guess which part of the body there is a contact meant to trigger or ask friends if they something different on their avatar. \n\nIn my case, I wanted to tell in the menu options 3 things like, speed, length and type of animation of a toggle but I couldn't tell much just with the Icon so I have to put text inside the icon.\n\nPlease create a tool tip for the action menu for a better UX!\n\nCheers!",
